claim("The minimal free-reed model (one-mode reed equation z'' + (w0/Q) z' + w0^2 z = mu*dp with mu = Sr/M, pumped flow Sr*z', jet flow alpha*Su(h)*vj with dp = rho*vj^2/2, an upstream volume V1 obeying (V1/c0^2) dp1/dt = rho*(u0 - u) and an upstream pipe obeying p1 = p2 + rho*(L2/S2) du/dt) self-oscillates when integrated with a semi-implicit Euler scheme at 352.8 kHz, using the published harmonica-reed parameters (Lr 12.95 mm, Wr 2.1 mm, er 110 um, es 900 um, rest offset 528 um, hmin 50 um, fr 444 Hz, K 47.9 N/m, Q 95; S0 30 mm2, S1 800 mm2, L2 20 mm, S2 25 mm2).",
      "software", True, [("millot", "section 2.1 eq. (4); section 2.2 eqs (5)-(7); section 3.1 equation list; Tables 2 and 3; appendix 5.2 and 5.4"), ("s03", "runs v0 = 1.5 to 3.5 m/s")], "verified", ["D-010", "D-011", "T-100", "T-101"], "not-in-input", "The spike used the Debut/Millot useful-section law, not the refined law of section 2.3.2.", FR)
claim("In that model there is a threshold supply flow below which the reed does not sound (silent at 1.0 m/s, sounding at 1.5 m/s supply velocity through 30 mm2), the sounding frequency lies below the reed's natural frequency (440.7 Hz against 444 Hz, -13 cents) and falls slightly as the supply rises (-13.0 to -13.8 cents from 1.5 to 3.5 m/s), the tip amplitude grows with supply (1.3 to 2.4 mm), and at a much larger fixed supply flow (4 m/s) the reed is pushed through the plate and stops.",
      "numerical", True, [("s03", "runs list"), ("millot", "section 3.2, figures 10 to 17 (qualitative agreement)")], "verified", ["D-011", "T-101", "T-102", "T-103"], "partly-supported", "The input file says pitch 'drops flat under excessive airflow'; the model shows a small fall and then choking. Measured cents-per-pascal figures for real reeds were not found.", FR)
claim("In that model the reed tip motion stays close to sinusoidal (second harmonic of the displacement between -53 and -43 dB) while the volume flow through the reed carries strong harmonics that grow with the supply (second harmonic of the flow from -18.5 dB to -8.9 dB re the fundamental), so the harmonic content of the sound comes from the flow law, not from the reed motion.",
      "numerical", True, [("s03", "flow_harmonics_dB, reed_h2_dB"), ("millot", "section 2.1 first paragraph; section 3.3")], "verified", ["D-011", "T-104"], "supported", "", FR)
